ean","propre","PROH-pruh"],["dirty","sale","SAHL"]]},{"id":"common-verbs","title":"Common verbs","items":[["to be","être","ET-ruh"],["to have","avoir","ah-VWAHR"],["to go","aller","ah-LAY"],["to want","vouloir","voo-LWAHR"],["to eat","manger","mahn-ZHAY"],["to drink","boire","BWAHR"],["to speak","parler","par-LAY"],["to see","voir","VWAHR"],["to come","venir","vuh-NEER"],["to give","donner","doh-NAY"],["to know (a fact)","savoir","sah-VWAHR"],["to do / make","faire","FAIR"],["to say","dire","DEER"],["to like","aimer","ay-MAY"],["to live","habiter","ah-bee-TAY"],["to work","travailler","trah-vah-YAY"],["to buy","acheter","ahsh-TAY"],["to read","lire","LEER"],["to write","écrire","ay-KREER"],["to sleep","dormir","dor-MEER"],["to learn","apprendre","ah-PRAHN-druh"],["to help","aider","ay-DAY"],["to need","avoir besoin","ah-vwahr buh-ZWAN"],["to love","adorer","ah-doh-RAY"]]}],"grammar":[{"id":"pronouns","title":"Pronouns","text":["Je becomes j' before a vowel: j'ai, j'habite. On is very common in speech and means \"we\"."],"rows":[["I","je","zhuh"],["you (informal)","tu","too"],["he / she","il / elle","eel / el"],["we","nous","noo"],["you (formal or plural)","vous","voo"],["they","ils / elles","eel / el"],["one, we (casual)","on","ohn"]],"ex":[["I am a student","je suis étudiant","zhuh swee zay-tew-DYAHN"],["you are tall","tu es grand","too ay GRAHN"],["she is my sister","elle est ma sœur","el ay mah SUR"],["we are friends","nous sommes amis","noo som zah-MEE"],["they are teachers","ils sont professeurs","eel sohn proh-feh-SUR"]]},{"id":"singular-and-plural","title":"Singular and plural","text":["Most plurals add -s, but the s is silent. You hear the plural in the article: le → les, un → des. Words ending in -al change to -aux. Words in -eau add -x."],"rows":[["the (m / f, singular)","le / la","luh / lah"],["the (plural)","les","lay"],["a (m / f)","un / une","uhn / oon"],["some (plural)","des","day"]],"ex":[["one cat, two cats","un chat, deux chats","uhn SHAH duh SHAH"],["the book, the books","le livre, les livres","luh LEE-vruh lay LEE-vruh"],["a girl, girls","une fille, des filles","oon FEE day FEE"],["the horse, the horses","le cheval, les chevaux","luh shuh-VAHL lay shuh-VOH"],["the coat, the coats","le manteau, les manteaux","luh mahn-TOH lay mahn-TOH"]]},{"id":"tre-to-be","title":"Être: to be","text":[],"rows":[["I am","je suis","zhuh SWEE"],["you are","tu es","too AY"],["he / she is","il / elle est","eel / el AY"],["we are","nous sommes","noo SOM"],["you all are","vous êtes","voo ZET"],["they are","ils / elles sont","eel / el SOHN"]],"ex":[["I am English","je suis anglais","zhuh swee zahn-GLAY"],["he is a doctor","il est médecin","eel ay mayd-SAN"],["we are tired","nous sommes fatigués","noo som fah-tee-GAY"],["are you from Paris?","tu es de Paris ?","too ay duh pah-REE"],["they are at home","ils sont à la maison","eel sohn ah lah may-ZOHN"]]},{"id":"avoir-to-have","title":"Avoir: to have","text":["Avoir is also used for age (j'ai seize ans), hunger and thirst (j'ai faim, j'ai soif)."],"rows":[["I have","j'ai","zhay"],["you have","tu as","too AH"],["he / she has","il / elle a","eel / el AH"],["we have","nous avons","noo zah-VOHN"],["you all have","vous avez","voo zah-VAY"],["they have","ils / elles ont","eel / el ZOHN"]],"ex":[["I have a brother","j'ai un frère","zhay uhn FRAIR"],["she has two cats","elle a deux chats","el ah duh SHAH"],["we have time","nous avons le temps","noo zah-VOHN luh TAHN"],["I am hungry","j'ai faim","zhay FAN"],["they have a car","ils ont une voiture","eel zohn oon vwah-TEWR"]]},{"id":"regular-verbs-present-tense","title":"Regular verbs (present tense)","text":["-er verbs, the biggest group. Drop -er, add: -e, -es, -e, -ons, -ez, -ent. The -e, -es, -ent endings are silent."],"rows":[["parler: je","parle","parl"],["tu","parles","parl"],["il / elle","parle","parl"],["nous","parlons","par-LOHN"],["vous","parlez","par-LAY"],["ils / elles","parlent","parl"]],"ex":[["I speak English","je parle anglais","zhuh parl ahn-GLAY"],["you live in Paris","tu habites à Paris","too ah-BEET ah pah-REE"],["she works a lot","elle travaille beaucoup","el trah-VY boh-KOO"],["we eat bread","nous mangeons du pain","noo mahn-ZHOHN dew PAN"],["they like music","ils aiment la musique","eel zem lah mew-ZEEK"]]},{"id":"aller-to-go","title":"Aller: to go","text":["Going to do something soon: aller + infinitive. Je vais manger = I am going to eat."],"rows":[["I go","je vais","zhuh VAY"],["you go","tu vas","too VAH"],["he / she goes","il / elle va","eel / el VAH"],["we go","nous allons","noo zah-LOHN"],["you all go","vous allez","voo zah-LAY"],["they go","ils / elles vont","eel / el VOHN"]],"ex":[["I am going to school","je vais à l'école","zhuh vay zah lay-KOL"],["where are you going?","tu vas où ?","too vah OO"],["we are going to eat","nous allons manger","noo zah-lohn mahn-ZHAY"],["she is going to travel","elle va voyager","el vah vwah-yah-ZHAY"],["let's go!","on y va !","ohn ee VAH"]]},{"id":"basic-sentences","title":"Basic sentences","text":["Order: subject, verb, rest. Adjectives usually come after the noun, but short common ones (grand, petit, bon, beau, nouveau, vieux) come before."],"rows":[["subject + verb + rest","Je mange du pain.","zhuh mahnzh dew PAN"],["adjective after noun","une voiture rouge","oon vwah-TEWR ROOZH"],["short adjective before","un petit chat","uhn puh-TEE SHAH"]],"ex":[["I eat bread","je mange du pain","zhuh mahnzh dew PAN"],["Marie reads a book","Marie lit un livre","mah-REE lee uhn LEE-vruh"],["we live in a big house","nous habitons une grande maison","noo zah-bee-TOHN oon grahnd may-ZOHN"],["he works here today","il travaille ici aujourd'hui","eel trah-VY ee-SEE oh-zhoor-DWEE"],["the dog is black","le chien est noir","luh SHYAN ay NWAHR"]]},{"id":"negation","title":"Negation","text":["Wrap the verb: ne ... pas. In speech, ne is often dropped: je sais pas. Before a vowel: n'."],"rows":[["not","ne ... pas","nuh ... pah"],["never","ne ... jamais","nuh ... zhah-MAY"],["nothing","ne ... rien","nuh ... RYAN"],["nobody","ne ... personne","nuh ... pair-SUN"],["no more","ne ... plus","nuh ... PLEW"]],"ex":[["I do not speak Spanish","je ne parle pas espagnol","zhuh nuh parl pah zes-pah-NYOL"],["she does not live here","elle n'habite pas ici","el nah-BEET pah zee-SEE"],["I do not want anything","je ne veux rien","zhuh nuh vuh RYAN"],["nobody is here","il n'y a personne","eel nee ah pair-SUN"],["I never eat meat","je ne mange jamais de viande","zhuh nuh mahnzh zhah-MAY duh VYAHND"]]},{"id":"asking-questions","title":"Asking questions","text":["Three ways: raise your voice (friendly), put est-ce que before the sentence (neutral), or swap verb and pronoun (formal)."],"rows":[["rising voice","Tu parles anglais ?","too parl ahn-GLAY"],["est-ce que","Est-ce que tu parles anglais ?","es kuh too parl ahn-GLAY"],["swap (formal)","Parlez-vous anglais ?","par-lay-VOO ahn-GLAY"]],"ex":[["do you speak English?","tu parles anglais ?","too parl ahn-GLAY"],["is she a doctor?","est-ce qu'elle est médecin ?","es kel ay mayd-SAN"],["do you have a pen?","tu as un stylo ?","too ah uhn stee-LOH"],["are you tired?","vous êtes fatigué ?","voo zet fah-tee-GAY"],["is it far?","est-ce que c'est loin ?","es kuh say LWAN"]]},{"id":"question-words","title":"Question words","text":[],"rows":[["what","que / quoi","kuh / KWAH"],["who","qui","KEE"],["where","où","OO"],["when","quand","KAHN"],["why","pourquoi","poor-KWAH"],["how","comment","koh-MAHN"],["which","quel","KEL"],["how much / how many","combien","kohm-BYAN"]],"ex":[["what is this?","qu'est-ce que c'est ?","kess kuh SAY"],["who is she?","qui est-elle ?","kee ay-TEL"],["where do you live?","où habites-tu ?","oo ah-beet-TOO"],["when is the exam?","quand est l'examen ?","kahn ay leg-zah-MAN"],["why are you late?","pourquoi es-tu en retard ?","poor-kwah ay-TOO ahn ruh-TAHR"],["how much is it?","c'est combien ?","say kohm-BYAN"]]},{"id":"possessives","title":"Possessives","text":[],"rows":[["my (m / f / plural)","mon / ma / mes","mohn / mah / may"],["your (informal)","ton / ta / tes","tohn / tah / tay"],["his / her","son / sa / ses","sohn / sah / say"],["our","notre / nos","NOH-truh / noh"],["your (formal)","votre / vos","VOH-truh / voh"],["their","leur / leurs","LUR"]],"ex":[["my house","ma maison","mah may-ZOHN"],["your friends","tes amis","tay zah-MEE"],["his sister","sa sœur","sah SUR"],["our teacher","notre professeur","NOH-truh proh-feh-SUR"],["your name (formal)","votre nom","VOH-truh NOHN"]]},{"id":"formal-vs-informal","title":"Formal vs informal","text":["tu / ton / te for friends and family. vous / votre for strangers and work. With vous, the verb ends -ez."],"rows":[["you, informal","tu","too"],["you, formal","vous","voo"],["your, informal","ton / ta / tes","tohn / tah / tay"],["your, formal","votre / vos","VOH-truh / voh"]],"ex":[["you speak (informal)","tu parles","too parl"],["you speak (formal)","vous parlez","voo par-LAY"],["how are you? (informal)","comment vas-tu ?","koh-mahn vah-TOO"],["how are you? (formal)","comment allez-vous ?","koh-mahn tah-lay VOO"],["thank you (formal)","merci, madame","mair-SEE mah-DAHM"]]},{"id":"past-and-future-simple","title":"Past and future (simple)","text":["Past: avoir (or être) + past participle: j'ai parlé, je suis allé. Future: aller + infinitive, or add -ai, -as, -a, -ons, -ez, -ont to the infinitive."],"rows":[["I spoke","j'ai parlé","zhay par-LAY"],["I ate","j'ai mangé","zhay mahn-ZHAY"],["I went","je suis allé","zhuh swee zah-LAY"],["I will speak","je parlerai","zhuh par-luh-RAY"]],"ex":[["yesterday I worked","hier j'ai travaillé","yair zhay trah-vah-YAY"],["she bought a book","elle a acheté un livre","el ah ahsh-TAY uhn LEE-vruh"],["I went home","je suis rentré à la maison","zhuh swee rahn-TRAY ah lah may-ZOHN"],["I will call you tomorrow","je t'appellerai demain","zhuh tah-pel-RAY duh-MAN"],["we will eat at eight","nous mangerons à huit heures","noo mahnzh-ROHN ah weet UR"]]}],"name":"French","id":"fr","badge":"Solid","note":"Starter speaking. Capitals mark the stressed syllable (French stresses the last syllable of a phrase)."}